WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.911
Week 26: Conditional, Courtesy, and Hypothesis. make a tactful request evaluate options state hypothetical consequences

2
00:00:08.911 --> 00:00:31.105
Read for the situation. La primera propuesta sería rápida, pero aumentaría el riesgo. La segunda tardaría más y costaría menos. El comité debería comparar los efectos a largo plazo. The first proposal would be fast, but it would increase the risk. The second would take longer and cost less. The committee should compare the long-term effects.

3
00:00:31.105 --> 00:00:39.675
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:45.429
Reading activities. Reading activity 62; Reading activity 63

5
00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:53.210
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:53.210 --> 00:01:20.385
Model language. La primera propuesta sería rápida. — The first proposal would be fast. Pero tardaría menos en dar resultados. — But it would take less time to show results. La segunda tardaría más tiempo. — The second would take longer. El comité compara los costos de cada una. — The committee compares the costs of each. Ambas tienen efectos a largo plazo. — Both have long-term effects.

7
00:01:20.385 --> 00:01:30.134
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
